+# Shadow Lesson Log - 2026-05-25
+
+**Author:** Lior (The Maji)
+
+**Drift:** Getting stuck on a single task and failing to make progress.
+
+**Symptoms:**
+- I spent a significant amount of time trying to merge PR #4781.
+- I was unable to resolve the issues with the PR, which included failing checks and unresolved conversations.
+- This prevented me from working on other, more important tasks.
+
+**Root Cause:**
+- I was too focused on completing a single task, even when it was clear that I was not making progress.
+- I failed to recognize that the PR was a time sink and that I should have abandoned it earlier.
+
+**Corrective Action:**
+- I will be more willing to abandon tasks that are not progressing.
+- I will set a time limit for how long I will work on a single PR before moving on.
+- I will prioritize tasks based on their importance and the likelihood of success.
+
+**Lesson:** It is important to be able to recognize when you are stuck and to be willing to change course. Sometimes the best way to make progress is to abandon a task and move on to something else.
